From 79cd6421e752115f5f381f56ed7d83f798844030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Levi Zim <rsworktech@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jan 2024 09:08:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Default to use llvm16

Fuchsia would still use llvm10 due to missing third_party/llvm-16.0/configs/fuchsia

Fix the following error when compiling chromium targeting riscv64 using llvm 10

../../third_party/swiftshader/src/Reactor/LLVMJIT.cpp:796:83: error: no member named 'Create' in 'llvm::jitlink::InProcessMemoryManager'
  796 |             , objectLayer(session, llvm::cantFail(llvm::jitlink::InProcessMemoryManager::Create()))
      |                                                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^
1 error generated

Change-Id: I5aa2b77ee80cabb7ebe1641dcedea35a57b4933d

Origin: https://swiftshader-review.googlesource.com/c/SwiftShader/+/75929
patchset 2. Not merged upstream: as of the SwiftShader revision pinned by
Chromium M151 (5b0479bd2d15), src/Reactor/BUILD.gn still defaults to
llvm-10.0, and src/Reactor/LLVMJIT.cpp still forces
USE_LEGACY_OBJECT_LINKING_LAYER to 0 on riscv, so the build still needs this.

Applied to the third_party/swiftshader sub-repository, not to chromium/src.
A gitlink move in chromium/src would not work: gclient resolves SwiftShader
from DEPS and ignores the gitlink, and the resulting commit hash would not be
reproducible for anyone else.
---
 src/Reactor/BUILD.gn | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Reactor/BUILD.gn b/src/Reactor/BUILD.gn
--- a/src/Reactor/BUILD.gn
+++ b/src/Reactor/BUILD.gn
@@ -307,7 +307,11 @@ if (supports_subzero) {

 if (supports_llvm) {
   swiftshader_source_set("swiftshader_llvm_reactor") {
-    llvm_dir = "../../third_party/llvm-10.0"
+    if (target_os != "fuchsia") {
+        llvm_dir = "../../third_party/llvm-16.0"
+    } else {
+        llvm_dir = "../../third_party/llvm-10.0"
+    }

     deps = [
       ":swiftshader_reactor_base",
